<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mexico"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mexico.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mexico</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">NAFTA comes into force and the Zapatistas rise in Chiapas</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Yemen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Yemen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Northern forces defeat a southern secession and take Aden</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20South%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of South Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first democratic elections make Nelson Mandela president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/anti-apartheid-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anti-apartheid%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anti-apartheid movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">South Africa holds its first election open to all, and Mandela becomes president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/azerbaijan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Azerbaijan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Azerbaijan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The First Nagorno-Karabakh War ends with Armenians holding 14–16 percent of Azerbaijani territory; in September SOCAR signs a 30-year contract with 13 oil companies.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/armenia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Armenia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Armenia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A Russian-brokered ceasefire ends the First Nagorno-Karabakh War, with some 30,000 dead and over a million displaced.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/uzbekistan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Uzbekistan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Uzbekistan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Oliy Majlis replaces the Supreme Soviet, the Republican Stock Exchange opens and Uzbekistan applies to join the World Trade Organization.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rwanda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rwanda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rwanda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 6 April Habyarimana's plane is shot down near Kigali; within hours the genocide begins, killing 500,000 to 1,000,000 Tutsi and moderate Hutu in about 100 days.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rwanda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rwanda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rwanda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The RPF takes control of the whole country, ending the genocide; some two million Hutu flee to Zaïre and other neighbours.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-haiti"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Haiti.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Haiti</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operation Uphold Democracy: 20,000 US troops enter Haiti and Jean-Bertrand Aristide, overthrown by Raoul Cédras's coup of 1991, is restored.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/khoekhoe"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Khoekhoe.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Khoekhoe</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Apartheid ends, and with it the racial designation “Coloured” imposed on some Khoekhoe</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/hoabinhian"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hoabinhian.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hoabinhian</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A conference in Hanoi votes to keep the term and to call the Hoabinhian an industry of the late Pleistocene to mid Holocene</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/nelson-mandela"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nelson%20Mandela.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nelson Mandela</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The ANC wins 63% of the vote in the first multiracial general election, and he is inaugurated as President of South Africa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/kyoto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kyoto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kyoto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Seventeen historic monuments of Kyoto are inscribed as World Heritage Sites</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/jericho"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jericho.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jericho</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Administrative control of Jericho passes to the Palestinian Authority</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/cape-town"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Cape%20Town.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Cape Town</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first democratic election is held on 27 April</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/sistine-chapel-ceiling"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sistine%20Chapel%20ceiling.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sistine Chapel ceiling</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Pope John Paul II unveiled the restored ceiling</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/nazca-lines"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazca%20Lines.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazca Lines</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">UNESCO designated the area a World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/potala-palace"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Potala%20Palace.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Potala Palace</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The palace was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List after restoration works between 1989 and 1994</span></li></ul></section>
